WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.426
Here is how to bring an avatar you already own into VR Vlog.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:15.684
Use a Unity 2022.3 project that already contains your avatar and lilToon.

3
00:00:15.684 --> 00:00:19.851
Install VR Vlog on your phone beforehand.

4
00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:24.396
First, save your work with File > Save.

5
00:00:24.396 --> 00:00:29.979
Close Unity with the top-right close button before installing the package.

6
00:00:30.884 --> 00:00:37.711
Open the official Exporter website linked below and select Install the exporter.

7
00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:43.806
Follow only the instructions for the manager you use: ALCOM or VCC.

8
00:00:43.806 --> 00:00:50.426
Both follow the same flow: register the repository, install into your project, then open Unity.

9
00:00:51.352 --> 00:00:57.133
For ALCOM, select ALCOM, then Add to ALCOM.

10
00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:02.915
For VCC, select VCC, then Add to VCC.

11
00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:10.287
If your browser asks for confirmation, check the manager's name and select Open.

12
00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:14.240
The repository information is sent to the manager automatically.

13
00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:19.797
Check the repository name and official URL, then add it.

14
00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:26.182
If it says the repository is already registered, continue to the next step.

15
00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.157
Return to the project list.

16
00:01:29.157 --> 00:01:36.698
For the project containing your avatar, select Manage in ALCOM or Manage Project in VCC.

17
00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:46.148
Find VR Vlog lilToon VRM Exporter in the package list.

18
00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:51.701
If you cannot find it, enter VR Vlog in the search field.

19
00:01:52.621 --> 00:01:55.803
In ALCOM, open None under Installed.

20
00:01:55.803 --> 00:02:04.237
In VCC, open Not Installed under Installed Version and select the latest stable version.

21
00:02:05.155 --> 00:02:09.681
In ALCOM, review the changes and select Apply.

22
00:02:09.681 --> 00:02:13.263
In VCC, installation starts when you select a version.

23
00:02:13.263 --> 00:02:15.715
Wait for it to finish.

24
00:02:16.622 --> 00:02:22.403
Installation is complete when the selected version appears in the Installed column.

25
00:02:23.322 --> 00:02:28.811
Select Open Unity in ALCOM or Open Project in VCC.

26
00:02:28.811 --> 00:02:32.965
Once Unity has finished loading, the remaining steps are the same.

27
00:02:33.889 --> 00:02:39.267
In the Hierarchy on the left, right-click the avatar's root object.

28
00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:44.972
Select the whole avatar, rather than a child object such as hair or clothing.

29
00:02:45.889 --> 00:02:52.225
From the VR Vlog menu, select Transfer to app (Easy).

30
00:02:53.156 --> 00:02:58.764
Check that the Avatar field and preview show the avatar you want to use.

31
00:02:58.764 --> 00:03:02.393
Enter the name you want to display in the app.

32
00:03:03.323 --> 00:03:07.218
Enter the avatar creator's name in the Author field.

33
00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:10.928
For this Kipfel example, the creator is もち山金魚.

34
00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:18.203
Open the VRM usage permissions and set them according to the avatar and outfit licenses.

35
00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:22.555
You do not need to copy the values shown in this video.

36
00:03:23.457 --> 00:03:27.382
After checking, tick the consent box at the bottom.

37
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:34.149
Connect your PC and phone to the internet, then select Create QR code.

38
00:03:34.149 --> 00:03:37.496
Wait for the export and transfer preparation to finish.

39
00:03:38.425 --> 00:03:42.841
When it is ready, a Show QR button appears.

40
00:03:42.841 --> 00:03:47.427
Select it to display the code for scanning.

41
00:03:48.359 --> 00:03:52.588
Use your phone's camera to scan the code on your own PC.

42
00:03:52.588 --> 00:03:55.250
The code itself is hidden in this video.

43
00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.756
Do not show your code to anyone else.

44
00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:02.818
Open VR Vlog from the link that appears.

45
00:04:02.818 --> 00:04:07.340
Check the file on the confirmation screen and select Receive.

46
00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.595
Wait until the transfer is complete.

47
00:04:11.526 --> 00:04:16.180
Once received, select your avatar and check its appearance.

48
00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:19.760
You can now film with your usual avatar.

49
00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:25.122
The following section is for cases where the Add button does not open the manager.

50
00:04:25.122 --> 00:04:29.728
You can also use this method if the wrong manager opens.

51
00:04:29.728 --> 00:04:33.802
If the normal Add button worked, you can skip this section.

52
00:04:34.727 --> 00:04:39.618
On the official website, expand When the manager does not open.

53
00:04:39.618 --> 00:04:43.192
Copy the repository URL shown there.

54
00:04:43.192 --> 00:04:46.577
The same URL is also linked below the video.

55
00:04:47.494 --> 00:04:52.969
In ALCOM, select the box icon on the left, then open VPM Repositories.

56
00:04:52.969 --> 00:04:57.947
In VCC, open Settings, then Packages.

57
00:04:58.861 --> 00:05:01.855
In ALCOM, select Add VPM Repository.

58
00:05:01.855 --> 00:05:05.794
In VCC, select Add Repository.

59
00:05:06.728 --> 00:05:13.810
In either manager, paste the official repository URL linked below and select Add.

60
00:05:14.728 --> 00:05:21.199
After registering the repository, continue from Install into your project in the main tutorial.

61
00:05:21.199 --> 00:05:26.376
If it says the repository is already registered, continue as well.

62
00:05:27.295 --> 00:05:32.104
You only need to register the repository and install the package once.

63
00:05:32.104 --> 00:05:38.516
Next time, start from Transfer to app (Easy) in Unity.
